%description:
Tests that the override timeout of the sender SWS avoidance (RFC 9293 section
3.8.6.2.1, rule (4)) expires while the peer sends data. The setup is that of
tcp_sws_2.test: the server offers 3500 bytes and reads nothing, so after three
segments its window is 500 bytes, and the client holds the rest of its data.
Here the server also sends 100 bytes every 0.3 s, shorter than the RTO of 1 s.
Each of its segments acknowledges SND.UNA with the same window of 500 bytes, so
it updates no window and must not restart the override timer: the client sends
the 500 bytes one RTO after the hold, at 2.2 s, as in tcp_sws_2.test, and not
only after the server stops sending (BD-21 of baseline-catch-up-defects.md).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 6s
*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 5000"
*.srv_app.sendScript="1.35 100; 1.65 100; 1.95 100; 2.25 100; 2.55 100; 2.85 100; 3.15 100; 3.45 100; 3.75 100; 4.05 100"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1000
*.srv_tcp.advertisedWindow = 3500
*.srv_app.autoRead=false

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains-regex: postrun-command(1).out
\[2\.2\d\d A\d+\] A\.1000 > B\.2000: A 3001:3501\(500\)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
PERSIST timer expired with an open window: overriding the SWS avoidance
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
